Calc: row heights evaluate a conditional format formula once per row when it cannot depend on the column.

The optimal row height pass (GetOptimalHeightsInColumn) asks every cell of every column for its
conditional format result, so an expression rule over many columns like `$F2>0.05` on A2:O60000 was
evaluated once per cell although its result is the same in every column of the row. While the pass
runs (ScDocument::CondRowCacheScope), ScConditionEntry::Interpret keeps the results of its relative
formulas per (sheet, row) when the formula has only absolute-column references, values, operators and
functions: names, labels, table/database/external references, ROW, COLUMN, CELL, OFFSET, INDIRECT,
SHEET, INFO, CURRENT, MULTIPLE.OPERATIONS and volatile formulas keep the per-cell evaluation. The cache
is dropped when the pass ends (a new pass id) and wherever the compiled formula is dropped.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_sc_ucalc_condformat testCondFormatRowResultsInRowHeightPass, CppunitTest_sc_condformats;
the row heights of the synthetic .xlsx files are byte-identical with and without the patch.
